                <pb facs="0730" n="606" sameAs="frus:frus1921v01/pg606"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.77/2233</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Harvey</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-09-28"><hi rendition="#italic">September 28,
                        1921</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 171</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The Department has received your despatch
                    No. 400 of August 24, 1921, enclosing a note from the British Foreign Office
                    relative to the reorganization of the supervision of the Chinese Eastern
                    Railway.</p>
                <p>You may inform the British Foreign Office that the Government intends to take up
                    this matter with the Chinese Government but has deemed it advisable, first, to
                    approach Japan. The answer from the Japanese Government is expected in the near
                    future.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Henry P.
                            Fletcher</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
